264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (The Campus Lost & Found Management System is a mobile application developed to make reporting and recovering lost items easier within a college campus. The application allows students to create accounts, report lost or found items, provide details such as item name, description, category, location, and date, and attach item photos. Firebase Authentication is used for secure user login and registration, while Cloud Firestore is used to store and manage item reports.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 228 0 R
/E (The system includes a matching feature that compares lost and found item details such as item name, description, category, location, date, and image information to identify possible matches. Users can view matching items and proceed with the claim and verification process. The application is developed using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose with Firebase services for backend functionality. Overall, the system provides a simple, organized, and efficient platform for managing lost and found items on campus and helps reduce the time required to recover misplaced belongings.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
