316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 232 0 R
/E (Existing lost and found systems mainly focus on reporting, searching, verification, and recovery of items. From the systems reviewed, there is limited emphasis on automatically comparing lost and found reports using multiple attributes such as item name, description, category, location, and date. This creates an opportunity for a campus-focused system that combines structured reporting with automated and explainable item matching. Our proposed system addresses this gap by generating match scores, confidence levels, and matching explanations to help users identify possible matches more efficiently. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
