322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 233 0 R
/E (The proposed Campus Lost & Found Item Matching System is developed as an Android mobile application that provides a centralized platform for managing lost and found items on campus. Users can securely register and log in using Firebase Authentication. After logging in, users can report a lost or found item by entering details such as item name, description, category, location, date, and photo. These records are stored in Cloud Firestore for easy access and management.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 233 0 R
/E (The system compares lost and found reports using a weighted multi-factor matching algorithm. It uses Jaccard similarity for keyword comparison and evaluates item name, description, category, location, and date proximity to generate a match score, confidence level, matched factors, and explanation. Possible matches are then displayed to the user. The application is developed using Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Firebase Authentication, and Cloud Firestore.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
